NAME
    coreutils - the standard command set (index)

SYNOPSIS
    (no such binary - see DESCRIPTION)

DESCRIPTION
    The basic operating-system tools used to be one busybox-style
    multi-call binary selected by argv[0]. They are now each a
    separate, self-contained executable in /bin:

        echo true false pwd cat ls mkdir rm touch uname clear
        wc head tail grep sort cp mv basename dirname seq df ping
        nohup

    There is no 'coreutils' program on the image any more; this
    page is kept as an index of the set. Run 'man <name>' for a
    single tool, or bare 'man' for every documented command.

    The separate account tools id, whoami, groups, useradd,
    passwd and su are standalone /bin binaries too. The disk
    installer is not one of them: it is 'vnu install' (see man vnu).
